cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CARD: Calibrating Accelerated Radiometric Decay"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Rick
    family-names: Sanders
repository-code: "https://github.com/creation-research-laboratory/card-model"
url: "https://creation-research-laboratory.github.io/card-model/"
abstract: >-
  A general model for accelerated radiometric decay within a young-earth
  creation framework. CARD represents the decay rate as a piecewise function of
  time, with accelerated periods during the Creation week and the Flood
  relaxing exponentially back toward the rate measured today, and converts
  between true young-earth ages and apparent secular ages. Model parameters can
  be specified, solved exactly from matched date pairs, or sampled with MCMC.
keywords:
  - radiometric dating
  - accelerated decay
  - young earth
  - creation science
  - geochronology
  - mcmc
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-01"
